Subject: [S] SPLUS procedures for Paired Survival Data
Message-ID: <B9E51B9719BDD111AB640000F80197CDBEB170@rplmsem2.pal.roche.com>

I have a clinical study where various patient side effects are recorded. Two
particular side effects are of interest, and for each effect I prepare a
time to "onset" of the side effect.  Can anyone suggest any SPLUS procedures
that are well suited to the analysis and interpretation of "paired" survival
data?  Perhaps there are some procedures for multivariate "time to event"
analysis available?

Thanks in advance.

Chris Barker, Ph.D.
