In-Reply-To: <B9E51B9719BDD111AB640000F80197CDBEB171@rplmsem2.pal.roche.com>
References: <B9E51B9719BDD111AB640000F80197CDBEB171@rplmsem2.pal.roche.com>
Message-ID: <Pine.GSO.4.05.9905020654030.1491-100000@auk.stats>

On Sat, 1 May 1999, Barker, Chris {GL P~Palo Alto} wrote:

> I'd like to estimate a regression equation such as, y =a +bx1 + cx2 +dx3
> where the estimates of the regression coefficients  (b,c,d) are constrained
> so that  (b>=c>=d)
> Is there any way in SPLUS to estimate such a regression with constraints?

nnls.fit (with a small re-parameterization as (a, d+e+f, d+e, d))
or nlregb (ditto).

Regression with linear constraints is a quadratic programming problem,
so you could use Berwin Turlach's quadprog library on statlib.

