>     V1 V2 V3 V4 V5 V6 V7 V8 V9 V10 V11 V12 V13 V14 V15 V16 Y 
> 999  1  1  2  1  1  7  7 12  1   7   6   8   3   8   0   8 H
> 
> 
> There must be a function that returns this "A".
> Could someone tell me what it is?

The `A' is just one choice of the most likely class. You haven't
told us the version of S-PLUS you are using. If you have a recent
version (3.4 or later) or my treefix library (from the V&R set)
you can use

predict(regtree,letter.recogn[999,], method="class")

Note that this chooses randomly amongst ties.  If you don't like that
(although it is good idea), edit which.is.max inside predict.tree to be
        which.is.max <- function(x)
        {
                y <- seq(length(x))[x == max(x)]
                y[1]
        }

See ?predict.tree for more details.

