Subject: Re: [S] union and intersection of sets
In-Reply-To: <Pine.SGI.3.96.990507155915.19482B-100000@sigma1.stat.washington.edu>
Message-ID: <Pine.SGI.3.96.990511113712.26844C-100000@sigma1.stat.washington.edu>

A few days ago I posted an intersect() function which I said was more
general than the one shipped with S+.  

Tim Hesterberg pointed out that my function fails when there's only one
argument, and offered one that doesn't.  Here it is.  

"intersect"<-
function(...)
{
        stuff <- lapply(list(...), unique)
        answer <- stuff[[1]]
        for(i in seq(along=stuff)[-1])
                answer <- answer[match(stuff[[i]], answer, nomatch = 0)]
        answer
}

