Thanks to all (too many to name here without forgetting someone important)
who responded to my "simple" questions.

1.  The short answer to the first question is (from Bill Venables):

names(dat)[32] <- "newA32"
names(dat)[match("XYX", names(dat))] <- "YXY"
whatever...

2.  Renaming a data.frame or matrix or list isn't possible directly.
Either it can be done in a function or via the paradigm I've been using all
along, i.e.

newname.df<-oldname.df
rm(oldname.df)

3.  dump/source vs. data.dump/data.restore.  My problem stemmed from clear
(but technically wrong) answer to the identical question given to a
colleague of mine, who in turn related it to me.  It looks like the only
way out of this problem for me now is to hand-edit all the "calls" inside
the various objects dumped to the ascii file.  Fortunately there were only
10 or 12 such beasts ( :-) ).  Contrary to the misinformation I was given,
data.dump and data.restore are the ticket here.  

Thanks again for the rapid responses.

