Even using help.start I can't figure out where I might change the
position of xlab and ylab in Trellis plots.  It's simple in "regular"
plots to use mtext and specify line = 1.5 (say).  

I know I can change the font size, the mgp parameter, etc used in the
axes by using the scales list in a trellis function.  What is the
corresponding method of changing just where xlab and ylab appear?

If there is only one trellis object, it's not difficult to make blank
labels and add mtext statements after the trellis object is printed.
Such an approach will not work if you want to keep the labels as part
of the trellis object which would be far more elegant.  

My primary school teacher would have asked 

axis : scales :: xlab : ?

Thank you

Patrick
