To the best of my knowledge there isn't a single source for a "manual" that
lists all the functions that SPlus offers in its stock installation.  Many
of the functions are completely undocumented in any of the formal printed
manuals so searching the .pdf versions is futile.  The only useful source
of on line information is the help files, but the problem with them is that
you actually need to know what you are looking for to find it.  

I would be content with a .pdf version of the reference manual (one page
per function in alphabetical order) that *I* could print off and put in a
binder.  Sometimes the only way to find something is to start browsing
linearly through a list of functions until you locate the one cryptically
named for the result you are seeking.  

