Depends on your version of S-PLUS. For Unix versions it is easy to
create a PS version of all the manual pages from the sources: for
example the V&R libraries have such a PS file in the on-line sources,
and this was essentially how the old reference manuals were prepared.

On Windows one is supposed to be able to print whole help files (which is
why the opening help screen for the add-on libraries I have ported
gives a `book' for the whole library) and although I have not tried the
S-PLUS library I have tried others. It seems to print each page separately.
Also, there are tools to turn .hlp files back into .rtf files which
could then be printed in Word or whatever: I tried that a long time ago on
the S-PLUS 3.3 help file and the tool crashed as the file was too big.

