On Thu, 13 May 1999, Mike Ernst wrote:

> 
> Prof Brian D Ripley wrote:
> > 
> > Depends on your version of S-PLUS. For Unix versions it is easy to
> > create a PS version of all the manual pages from the sources: for
> > example the V&R libraries have such a PS file in the on-line sources,
> > and this was essentially how the old reference manuals were prepared.
> 
> I am unfamiliar with how and where the manual pages are stored.  How
> would I go about doing this?

They are in .Data/.Help, except that for most system libraries it
is not .Data....

On S-PLUS 3.4 the system help is in

SHOME/s/.Functions/.Help
SHOME/s/.Datasets/.Help
SHOME/stat/.Functions/.Help
SHOME/stat/.Datasets/.Help
SHOME/splus/.Functions/.Help
SHOME/splus/.Datasets/.Help

Now, to produce printed help for the V&R libraries I use

auk% less Mkdoc
#!/bin/csh

unalias cd
unset time

rm -rf MASS class nnet spatial treefix
mkdir MASS class nnet spatial treefix

foreach dir (MASS class nnet spatial treefix)
echo -- installing in $dir
cp ../../soft/$dir/help/*.d $dir
cd $dir
../nr2doc $dir
cd ..
end

rm -f VR3help.zip
zip -lj9 VR3help README */*.rtf
rm -rf MASS class nnet spatial treefix

foreach dir (MASS class nnet spatial treefix)
  touch tmp.d
  foreach f (`ls ../../soft/$dir/help/*.d | sort -f`)
    cat $f >> tmp.d
    echo ".bp" >> tmp.d
  end
  cat tmp.d | PRINT >! $dir.ps
  rm tmp.d
end
tar cvf VR3help.tar *.ps
rm *.ps
gzip -f9 VR3help.tar

where PRINT is a modified form of the file in SHOME/cmd:

auk% cat PRINT
#!/bin/sh

PATH=$PATH:/usr/lib/lp/postscript

sed -e "/\`/s/\'/\\\\fP\\\\s+1/g
        /\`/s/\`/\\\\f3\\\\s-1/g"  |
    eqn |
    troff -Tpost help.tr - 2>/dev/null | dpost | postreverse -r

(specific to Solaris) and help.tr is there too.

Either that is enough to get you going or you will need an expert
on your OS.

