Message-ID: <199905141048.MAA28653@gwen.stat.unipd.it.>

For the noncentral t, I can offer a "near solution" in Splus:
the formualae of Owen (Biometrika 1965 p.437) are easy to implement
provided one can compute the function T(h,a) studied by Owen
in connection with the bivariate normal integral (AMS 1956, p.1075).

What I have available in Splus is a function T.Owen() which computes
this T(h,a).  This is part of the library(sn), freely available from
http://www.stat.unipd.it/dip/homes/azzalini/SN

With a little bit of extra Splus coding  one gets the noncentral 
t distribution.

best wishes
