> Solaris 2.6.1.
> Splus 5.0R3.
> 
> I do not have cc compiler so the following error occurs:
> 
> I would like to use gcc instead of cc. What is the simplest way to do it?

Change the $(SHOME)/library/S_FLAGS file. That has

CC=cc
CFLAGS=-I$${SHOME}/include  -Xa  $(LOCAL_CFLAGS) -O -KPIC

and you will need

CC=gcc
CFLAGS=-I$${SHOME}/include  $(LOCAL_CFLAGS) -O -fPIC

Having said that, adding those lines to the makefile after the line

include $(SHOME)/library/S_FLAGS

and running Splus5 make after Ins5 works for me.

