For the first question
i suppose that mat is the name of your matrix or data.frame
this the solution
dimnames(mat)[[2]]<-c("nom1",...,"nomN")
where N is the number of columns of your matrix (ncol(mat))
and nom1,..,nomN is the new names for the columns of your matrix

for the second problem
when you creates your matrix mat, you should probably use mat<<- ... instead
of
mat<- ...
in your program.In fact when you uses <<- instead of <- tho object will be
create in your
frame in which you works.

hope it helps, if this don't work say me please
best regards.
